{
  "dom_id": "step-q343187",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14096050/assets/6eb2c7621d7be454bb287325e97f2db47ddf6591d269b26df58ac65b8ee7ca5f.png)\n\nA rectangular fish tank is draining. The tank is $6\\,\\text{ft}$ long and $4\\,\\text{ft}$ wide. What is the rate of change of the water level if the volume is decreasing at a rate of $1.2\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}/\\text{min}?$ Assume that the water level's rate of decrease is positive.\n\nThe water level is decreasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{ft}/\\text{min}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the rectangular prism, let $V$ be its volume. We are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6\\,\\text{ft}, \\\\ y & =4\\,\\text{ft}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-1.2\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}/\\text{min}.\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}$ when $x=6\\,\\text{ft}$ and $y=4\\,\\text{ft}.$\n\nWe start with the formula for the volume of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nV=xyz\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known values, we get\n\n$$\nV=(6)(4)z=24z.\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(24z) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =24(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known value into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1.2 & =24(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} & =-0.05\\,\\text{ft}\\text{/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the water level is decreasing at a rate of $0.05\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{min}.$",
